questions.e:
```
public class ClientGuessRequest implements Serializable {
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 10L;
    final public int guess;
    public ClientGuessRequest(int guess) { this.guess = guess; }
}
```
Pola `final public` + konstruktor = niezmienny (immutable) komunikat. Różne `serialVersionUID` w klasach (1L, 2L, 10L, 11L) to etykiety wersji. Gdyby klient i serwer miały różne wersje klasy, odbiorca rzuciłby `InvalidClassException`. Enumy (`Evaluation`, `GameColor`) są serializowalne automatycznie.

questions.q:
Jak serwer losuje tajną liczbę?
```
static int generateSecretNumber(int fromIncluded, int toIncluded) {
    return new Random().nextInt((toIncluded - fromIncluded) + 1) + fromIncluded;
}
```

Serwer `ServerGuessingGame.start()`:
```
try (ServerSocket serverSocket = new ServerSocket(port)) {
    while (true) {
        Socket socketForClient = serverSocket.accept();
        Thread.startVirtualThread(() -> handleClient(socketForClient));
    }
}
```
Co robi `accept()` i po co osobny wątek?

Dlaczego w kliencie `ObjectOutputStream` jest tworzony PRZED `ObjectInputStream`, a w serwerze odwrotnie (najpierw `ObjectInputStream`)?
```
// klient: Socket s; out = new ObjectOutputStream(s.getOutputStream()); in = new ObjectInputStream(s.getInputStream());
// serwer: in = new ObjectInputStream(socket.getInputStream());         out = new ObjectOutputStream(socket.getOutputStream());
```

Klient:
```
try (Socket socket = new Socket(serverAddress, serverPort);
     ObjectOutputStream out = ...; ObjectInputStream in = ...) { ... }
catch (UnknownHostException ex) { ... }
catch (IOException ex) { ... }
catch (ClassNotFoundException ex) { ... }
```
Dlaczego `UnknownHostException` jest przed `IOException`?

Co robi klient w pętli?
```
ClientGuessRequest myGuess = ClientUtils.generateRandomGuess(gameRange);
while (true) {
    out.writeObject(myGuess); out.flush();
    ServerEvaluationResponse r = (ServerEvaluationResponse) in.readObject();
    if (r.result == HIT) break;
    myGuess = ClientUtils.generateRandomGuess(gameRange);
}
```

Jak serwer rozróżnia typ komunikatu od klienta?
```
Object request = in.readObject();
if (request instanceof ClientGameEnterRequest enterRequest) { ... }
else if (request instanceof ClientGuessRequest guessRequest) { ... }
```

